            <div xml:id="d252">

                <pb facs="0414" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg315"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 War Credits/726</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Greek
                        Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sicilianos</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-12">November 12, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At the request of the United States
                    Treasury Department, I have the honor to notify your Government that on November
                    6, 1936, there was deposited with the Federal Reserve Bank of New York for
                    credit to the account of the Treasurer of the United States, the sum of $87,168
                    by the Bank of Greece for account of the Government of Greece as a partial
                    payment of interest due from that Government to the United States. The Treasury
                    applied these funds to the payment of 40 percent of the semiannual interest
                    amounting to $217,920 due November 10, 1936, on the 4% loan of 1929.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
